edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342091 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1$ at the point $(1,1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342091 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f18efd9d-f823-53b1-9b52-0bc881b7962b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342091 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1) & =\\frac{1}{1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{1}{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1) \\\\ z-1 & =1\\cdot (x-1)+1\\cdot (y-1) \\\\ z-1 & =x+y-2 \\\\ -x-y+z+1 & =0 \\\\ x+y-z-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342093 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342093 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73851" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342093 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342093 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)$ at the point $(1,1,\\pi ,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342093 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de6bd964-56b9-511c-9d67-ed8d06732a08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342093 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))=yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))=xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,1,\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1,\\pi ) & =(1)(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi )=-\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1,\\pi ) & =(1)(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi )=-\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,1,\\pi ) & =(1)(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi )=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1,\\pi )+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1,\\pi )+(z-\\pi )\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,1,\\pi ) \\\\ w & =-\\pi (x-1)-\\pi (y-1)-(z-\\pi ) \\\\ w & =-\\pi x+\\pi -\\pi y+\\pi -z+\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x+\\pi y+z+w-3\\pi  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342095 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342095 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342095 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342095 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w={x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2}$ at the point $(1,-1,1,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342095 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4142a5f1-3da0-59f6-9d01-2beeae09fd8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342095 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2})=2xyz+{y}^{2}z+y{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2})={x}^{2}z+2xyz+x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}yz+x{y}^{2}z+xy{z}^{2})={x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}+2xyz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1) & =2(1)(-1)(1)+(-1)^{2}(1)+(-1)(1)^{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1) & =(1)^{2}(1)+2(1)(-1)(1)+(1)(1)^{2}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) & =(1)^{2}(-1)+(1)(-1)^{2}+2(1)(-1)(1)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-(-1) & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1)+(y-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) \\\\ w+1 & =-2(x-1)+0\\cdot (y+1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w+1 & =-2x-2z+4 \\\\ 2x+2z+w-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383111 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383111 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129435" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383111 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383111 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-7$ at the point $(1,-1,6).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383111 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58da2e0b-eb6e-5d08-a4d3-1469fcdda740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383111 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-7) \\\\  & =8x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-7) \\\\  & =18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1) & =8(1)=8 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1) & =18(-1)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-6 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1)+(y-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1) \\\\ z-6 & =8(x-1)-18(y+1) \\\\ z-6 & =8x-18y-26 \\\\ 8x-18y-z-20 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186383113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383112 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "facf18b7-00ac-5d4c-a780-571ce69d518f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383113 #edb/ref 1080 "8x-18y-z-20=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383113 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383113 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d75fcdf-fb78-57bb-b854-212e11099d6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383114 #edb/ref 1080 "8x+18y+z-16=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383114 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383114 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c6316d6-6422-54c0-86cd-72086b4081b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383115 #edb/ref 1080 "2x+3y-z+7=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417