al vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨2x+2,\\,2y+2,\\,-1⟩=⟨-4,0,1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}c(2x+2) &=-4 \\\\ c(2y+2) &=0 \\\\ -c &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-(2x+2)=-4\\,⟹\\,x=1.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n-(2y+2)=0\\,⟹\\,y=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =(1)^{2}+2(1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(1,-1,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385593 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fc46821c-d90f-57c3-87fa-76db78d17b0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385594 #edb/ref 1080 "$(1,1,6)$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385594 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385594 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "22adf989-5e2a-597b-819b-21a19def1126" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385595 #edb/ref 1080 "$(1,-1,2)$ and $(-1,1,2)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385595 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385595 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11941d78-